# Eval-script output artifacts (scripts themselves are committed; results aren't)
scripts/*.json

# SQLite databases — ALL of them, by extension, not by name.
#
# Naming individual files is what failed on 2026-08-03: elixir-telemetry.db was
# committed before its ignore rule existed, .gitignore does not untrack an
# already-tracked file, and 96 MB of LLM prompts and responses — including 11
# member email addresses — were pushed to this PUBLIC repository across five
# commits. A per-file rule only protects the files somebody remembered.
#
# No SQLite database belongs in this repo: they are large, rebuildable, and
# carry member data. The sidecar suffixes matter as much as the file — a -wal
# holds committed rows that are not yet in the main file.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db3
*.s3db
*.sl3

# AGENT-TEAM per-run scratch (roles' notes; noisy). Role defs, scripts, and the
# Manager's summaries/ ARE committed — only the raw run notes are ignored.
AGENT-TEAM/notes/

# Pre-v5.1 .env backup (secrets — never commit)
.env.pre-v51
run_enrich_live.sh
enrich_live.log
